title TACT-J2r3 — the receipt made portable (Bron round-trip)
prompt continue the road Lindy-first crux-first; keep agent-doable work moving; send each increment; stop at custody gates
think r1 (offline verify) and r2 (constellation-bound) proved a receipt's trust; r3 makes it travel. Renders a Publication to a format publication-v1 Bron record and parses it back byte-for-byte.
think The crux is preservation: parse(render(receipt)) recovers an equal receipt (point, name, len, digest, sig) and the recovered receipt still verify_offline's against the publisher's key — the signed word survived becoming text. digest/sig cross as lowercase hex (32B->64, 64B->128); point/len via tally parse_int; name flat.
think The reader is purpose-built and bounded: an unknown field refuses UnknownField (never dropped), a missing field MissingField, a wrong header BadFormat, malformed/short hex BadHex. Four cases green.
obs TAME ban caught before commit: inline `) == error.` at a call seam in the header/hex refusal test; bound each parse result to a const first (header_result/hex_result), matching the other unwelcome cases. tame_style_check then GREEN.
obs Reads no network — the serve transport carrying this record across the wire is the Comlink-served custody gate (r4). Journey 2's agent-doable arc (r1 offline · r2 bound · r3 portable) now stands; only the serve rung remains, and it is Keaton's hand.
